keeping you healthier while this is occurring remember it is almost time for the batteries in your smoke alarms and carbon monoxide alarms to be replaced so time to get them batteries smoke alarm should be placed in and outside every sleeping area and on every level of the home carbon monoxide alarms should be on every level of your home and outside sleeping areas additional carbon monoxide alarms are recommended 5 to 20 feet from any carbon monoxide producing appliances smoke and carbon monoxide alarms need to be checked for proper operation and if they're older than 10 years they should be replaced if you have any questions or need assistance with smoke and carbon monoxide alarms contact shine fire rescue at 307-637-6311 Cheyenne fire rescue wants you to be safe and

